# 1. THE MAIN VISION

OmniLab is an AI-powered interactive science learning and virtual experimentation platform for students, especially Classes 5–10 and students who have limited access to physical laboratories.

The main problem we are solving:

Students often learn STEM through textbooks, memorisation, formulas and theoretical explanations. Many students do not get enough opportunities to perform experiments, explore scientific concepts, change variables, test hypotheses and observe what actually happens.

This problem is particularly significant in rural and underserved schools where laboratory equipment, individual guidance and practical learning opportunities may be limited.

Our platform must transform students from passive learners into active scientific explorers.

Students should be able to:

1. Ask any scientific or academic question.
2. Understand the concept through a simple explanation.
3. See a relevant educational video or generated visual demonstration.
4. Learn how the experiment or concept works.
5. Create their own experimental setup.
6. Select and arrange virtual laboratory equipment.
7. Make predictions before running experiments.
8. Change variables and parameters.
9. Run scientifically supported simulations.
10. Observe results, graphs and measurements.
11. Compare multiple experiments.
12. Understand why results changed.
13. Generate educational videos for topics and problems.
14. Save, revisit and share their learning work safely.

The platform must support Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Mathematics, Computer Science, Engineering, Astronomy, Environmental Science and other STEM topics.

